================================================================================================================
HOW TO READ THIS
================================================================================================================
  Quote maker_taker. Entry is patient -- an unfilled post costs nothing --
  but the exit is not optional, so crossing it is the honest assumption.
  maker_maker assumes you can also leave whenever you like, which is the
  assumption that makes every maker backtest look good.

  Compare against taker_taker in the SAME table rather than against the
  earlier run: same events, same fill model, one difference.

  If maker_taker is positive, check three things before believing it:
    1. the fill rate -- a 5% fill rate on 2,366 signals is ~120 trades, and
       a positive mean over 120 trades needs its CI, not its point estimate;
    2. that --fill-model optimistic gives a MATERIALLY better number, which
       is what proves the fill rule was actually binding;
    3. that the win rate did not collapse relative to the taker row -- if it
       did, you are being filled on the wrong side and the profit is coming
       from the spread alone, which a real counterparty would not hand over.
